+// The destination slot for a binding narrowed to one member of its own union, when the slot that stores that
+// member is a shared shape struct. `{ outcome: 'destroyed' }` and `{ outcome: 'already-destroyed' }` are both
+// stored as one struct named for the shape `{ outcome }`; the narrowed member, spelled on its own, names a
+// literal-specific struct no value is stored as, so it matches no destination slot by spelling. What the binding's storage actually holds is the shared slot, and reading the
+// narrowed binding projects exactly that slot. So the value enters the destination slot of that same carrier
+// unchanged -- same object, no conversion -- and only when the answer is unique on both sides: the member is held
